  "content": "17 killed in landslides in Ilam\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 5, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 5\nAt least 17 people have been killed in landslides triggered by floods in Ilam district. Human casualties have been reported mostly in Ilam Municipality, Suryodaya Municipality, Deumai Municipality, Mangsebung Rural Municipality, and Phakphokthum Rural Municipality.\nIn Ilam Municipality-6, Ghos, six members of the family of Dambar Bahadur Tamang were killed after their house was buried by a landslide. A rescue team from the Armed Police Force’s Shree Antu Battalion was deployed to the site.\nSimilarly, in Suryodaya Municipality-1, Manebhanjyang, five people were killed when a landslide swept away the house of Raju Chhetri. Four bodies were recovered from the debris, while one injured person died on the way to hospital. A seven-member rescue team under the command of Armed Police Sub-Inspector Surendra Dotel was mobilized in the area.\nIn Deumai Municipality-5, Ghuseini, a landslide buried the house of Deepak Limbu, killing two people. Three others remain missing, while one person was rescued safely.\nLikewise, in Mangsebung Rural Municipality-5, three people died when a landslide struck the house of Madan Limbu.\nPolice also confirmed that in Phakphokthum Rural Municipality-3, Ratomate, 32-year-old Suresh Limbu was killed after being buried by a landslide.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nGen Z\nHate speech\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nLandslide clearance begins on Narayangadh- Muglin Road\n2 weeks ago\nMuglin-Narayangadh road closed for 38 hours as landslide clearance continues\n2 weeks ago\nBeni-Jomsom and Beni-Darbang roads obstructed by landslide\n2 months ago\nLandslide blocks Araniko Highway again\n2 months ago\nDumre-Ambukhaireni road section blocked by landslide\n2 months ago\n11 national highways completely blocked\n3 months ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nNepalis celebrate Bijaya Dashami, auspicious Tika time set at 11:53 am\nManaslu climbing in autumn starts on encouraging note; Nima Chhiring sets new record\nMonsoon triggers flood and landslide risks in several districts, DHM issues special alert\nClay and culture: The making of Durga idols\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n2 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n2 months ago\nAlso Read\nBlog\nWhen Nepal’s youth dared to dream of a better tomorrow\n14 hours ago\nSociety\nAI and fake accounts drove one third of online buzz during Nepal Gen Z uprising\n16 hours ago\nCricket\nIndu becomes first Nepali woman to score 1,000 runs in T20I cricket\n17 hours ago\nDisaster\nNighttime vehicle movement banned indefinitely on Hetauda–Kathmandu short route\n2 days ago\nDisaster\nHundreds stranded on Everest’s eastern side after heavy snowfall\n2 days ago",
